*added function /get_env_node_in/ in added file /Utils_node/
val get_env_node_in : Name.t -> 
    (Name.t * (Ast.Var.Set.t * Ast.Var.t list * Ast.Var.t list * (Name.t * (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list) list)) list ->
    Name.t -> Ast.expr list -> Location.t ->
    Ast.Var.Set.t * Ast.Var.t list * (Name.t * (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list) list
PrintResults, Utils_node : used
get_env_node e_id vars_node name args l returns the environment associated to e_id in vars_node with variables of args and external memory variables added, returns also the list of input variables of the node e_id and the map containing the relation between external and internal memory variables associated to each instances of node e_id
The list of input variables and the map are contained in vars_node associated to e_id.
example : 
 env1 = {(x,typx); (y,typy); (mem_int, typmem)}  m = {(sn1,([(mem_ext,(mem_int,typmem))]))}  ins = [(x,typx); (y,typy)]  vn = {(e_id,(env1,ins,outs,m))}  args = [u; (4 +m); 8]
 get_env_node_in e_id vn n args l = env2, ins, m with env2 = {(x,typx); (y,typy); (mem_int,typmem); (u ^ "_from_args", typx); (m ^ "_from_args", typy); (mem_ext, typmem)}



*added function /get_rel_in/ in added file /Utils_node/
val get_rel_in : Ast.expr list -> Ast.Var.t list -> (Name.t * (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list) list ->
    Name.t -> Name.t -> Location.t -> (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list
Utils_node : used
get_rel_in args inputs vars_of_args map name e_id l returns the relational map containing the relation between inputs and args, the relation between variables of args and suffixed variables of args, the relation between external and internal memory variables associated to name and the identity relation for external memory variables
example :
 a = [(a / 2)]  ins = [(x,typx)]  map = {(n1,([(g,(p_g,typg))])); (n2,([(h,(p_h,typh))]))}
 get_rel_in a ins map n1 id l = [(a/ 2, (x,typx)); (a,(a ^ "_from_args", typa); (g,(p_g,typg))]



*added function /get_env_rel_in/ in added file /Utils_node/
val get_env_rel_in : Name.t -> 
    (Name.t * (Ast.Var.Set.t * Ast.Var.t list * Ast.Var.t list * (Name.t * (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list) list)) list ->
    Name.t -> Ast.expr list -> Location.t -> (Ast.Var.Set.t * (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list)
get_env_rel_in e_id vars_nodes name args l returns the environment associated to node e_id and the entry relational map
Function get_env_rel_in simply calls get_env_node_in and get_rel_in then returns both results.



*added function /get_rel_out/ in added file /Utils_node/
val get_rel_out : Name.t -> 
    (Name.t * (Ast.Var.Set.t * Ast.Var.t list * Ast.Var.t list * (Name.t * (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list) list)) list ->
    Ast.expr list -> Name.t -> Name.t list -> Location.t -> (Ast.expr * Ast.Var.t) list
get_rel_out e_id vars_node args name l_returned_vars l returns the relational map containing the relation between returned values and assigned variables, between suffixed variables of args and variables of args and the relation between internal and external memory variables associated to name
